{
  "note": "What each retail cartridge that drives one of these parts is, so a copy you already own can be confirmed before it is read. Nothing here is any part of one: a digest identifies a file and no set of digests reconstructs anything.",
  "canonical": {
    "digest": "sha256 decides. crc32, md5 and sha1 are published beside it so a copy can be cross-checked against a database that keys on one of those, and none of them decides anything alone: crc32 is a 32-bit error code, and md5 and sha1 are both collision-broken.",
    "why": "A cartridge is read here for one thing: the routine inside it that drives the part. That routine states how many bytes go each way and how wide each transfer is, which is written down nowhere else.",
    "retailOnly": "Only retail releases are listed. A hack or a translation can carry altered code, so a driver routine read out of one would describe that edit rather than the part."
  },
